0f747d7b32e447b060","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831},{"symptom":"NUMBNESS","chapter":"teeth","parent":"LOOSENESS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"24a24f53589f4c070fb86b65","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831},{"symptom":"canines","chapter":"teeth","parent":"PAIN","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"edb183596dbc4be0a547b479","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831},{"symptom":"petr., phos., phos-ac, plat., ran","chapter":"teeth","parent":"PAIN","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"2a9a53cef49a121a47668805","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831},{"symptom":"sensation","chapter":"teeth","parent":"LOOSENESS","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"b53b59ee18400b51d0c58af0","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831},{"symptom":"FALL, tendency to","chapter":"vertigo","parent":"Carb-V., uit-ac, phos., plat","evidenceType":"repertory","source":"06_kent_repertory","evidenceRef":"f0ccccfe2ae23501138bc2a2","weight":1.0,"confidence":0.831}],"sections":[{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"mouth","label":"Mouth","startLine":29071,"endLine":29073,"text":"Scurvy; nursing sore mouth. [Veronica.]\nAphthous stomatitis."},{"source":"04_boericke_materia_medica","section":"relationship","label":"Relationship","startLine":29074,"endLine":29080,"text":"Said to be antidotal to the iction\nof Mercury, and has been employed in the treatment\nof .secondary syphilis after mercurialization.\n\n..^Dose. — Tincture. Usually locally to soft, spongy\nIjgiims, aphthae, pharyngitis, etc. Internally, first potency."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"mind","label":"Mind","startLine":20266,"endLine":20270,"text":"Distaste for society ; no desire to speak to any one, or to be\nspoken to (sixth day).—The sensorium was affected ; weakness of memory,\nmuch indifference to surrounding objects; sensation of stupidity (fourth\nand fifth days)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"head","label":"Head","startLine":20271,"endLine":20278,"text":"Awoke in the morning with a dull heavy headache, which\nwas dispelled by exercise, but again returned on resuming the use of the\ndrug (second day).—Severe cephalalgia (third day).—Headache until\nbreakfast, and a little in the afternoon (sixth day)/—-Dull aching pain in\nthe front and top of the head, for a short time after taking each dose\n(first day).—Fulness and pain in the top of the head (second day).—The\ndull heavy pain in vertex continues (fourth day)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"nose","label":"Nose","startLine":20279,"endLine":20292,"text":"*Hsemorrhage from the left nostril and mouth (fifth day).—\n[10.] Bloody scabs in the left nostril (sixth day).—Left nostril hot and\ndry, free haemorrhage from it three times during the latter part of the day ;\nthe prover is quite sure that the epistaxis is caused by the action of the\ndrug (seventh day).\n\nMonth. —Tongue furred white (fourth, fifth, and sixth days).—Several\nsmall ulcers form in the buccal mucous membrane, opposite the bicuspids\n(seventh day) ; the ulcers are very sensitive (eighth day) ; they were quite\nsensitive for several days, but healed kindly, except the largest, which was\ntouched with chloride of zinc (seventeenth day).—Could taste the drug in\nthe mouth thirty hours after the last dose was taken.—Mouth has a flat\nalkaline taste (fifth day)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"throat","label":"Throat","startLine":20293,"endLine":20295,"text":"Expelled two clots of blood from the throat, soon after wak¬\ning (sixth day)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"stomach","label":"Stomach","startLine":20296,"endLine":20302,"text":"Sensation of hunger (fourth day).—At breakfast could\neat but a little, although feeling as if he had fasted for many days (sixth\nday).—Loss of appetite, anorexia (third day).—[20.] Distress in stomach,\ndisturbed, very restless (third night).—Pain in the stomach aggravated\nby either food or drink, so much so as to cause the prover to nearly ab¬\nstain from their use (fourth and fifth days)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"abdomen","label":"Abdomen","startLine":20303,"endLine":20308,"text":"Cutting pain in the umbilical region for a few minutes\n(after first dose) ; constant (after second dose), (second day) ; the sharp cut¬\nting abdominal pains continue (eighth day).—Some tenderness on pressure\nin the umbilical region (fourth and fifth days).—Pain in the umbilical re¬\ngion (after second and third doses).—Pain in the bowels (third day)."},{"source":"08_allen_encyclopedia","section":"stool","label":"Stool","startLine":20309,"endLine":20317,"text":"Occasionally during the afternoon a diarrhoea, increasing in\nconstancy and severity towards evening ; at 7 p.m. a dry, hard stool (first\nday); no stool (second day) ; stool, first part hard and dry, the latter, soft\nand moist (third and fourth days) ; stool as usual, in the morning; another,\nhard and dry, in the evening (sixth day) ; stool nearly normal (seventh\nday) ; slight diarrhoea of short continuance (ninth day).\n\n330"}],"corpusPassages":[]}